            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 26 manifest paths from a risk lens (security, authorization, data exposure/loss, unsafe input, secrets, dependencies).",
              "The change is predominantly deletion: two GADU skill files, their registry entries, manifest rows and approval-baseline entries (engine/skills/approval_baseline.go), plus removal of sections A, E and F from skills/_shared/sdd-phase-common.md. These are prompt/documentation assets with no secrets, credentials, network calls or executable input handling.",
              "The approval baseline shrinks from 37 to 35 entries; the removed entries correspond exactly to the retired skills. This narrows the grandfathered set and does not weaken the approval gate for any remaining skill. The pinned count in engine/skills/approval_gate_test.go and the new engine/skills/gadu_skills_retired_test.go keep the registry, manifest and tree consistent.",
